{
  "id": "Compound::DB01291 - Gene::153",
  "verbalization": "Pirbuterol, a member of the adrenergic beta2-agonists class, is implicated in the interaction with Adrb1 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Pirbuterol binds to Adrb2, which in turn participates in beta-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately leading to interactions with Adrb1. This implies a potential role for Pirbuterol in modulating Adrb1 activity, possibly through the activation of beta-adrenergic signaling pathways. Additionally, the inclusion of Pirbuterol within the adrenergic beta2-agonists class, along with its binding to Adrb1 in some cases, suggests a broader pharmacological relationship that may involve the activation of beta-adrenergic receptors. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of beta-adrenergic signaling in the pharmacological effects of Pirbuterol, with Adrb1 potentially being a key target in this context.",
